WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:02.270
Continue the attack!

00:02.270 --> 00:03.560
That damn Million...

00:03.560 --> 00:06.730
...they will continue to suffer.

00:07.880 --> 00:10.320
I'm in love with Ouka?

00:10.320 --> 00:14.240
Recall what the true intent behind us being gathered was.

00:14.240 --> 00:18.580
They're all my names, yet none truly identifies me.

00:18.580 --> 00:20.830
Even this body. I don't know to whom it truly belongs to.

00:20.830 --> 00:21.820
Mom?

00:21.820 --> 00:24.010
Shut up! I'm insecure!

00:24.010 --> 00:26.790
I might not be myself, you know?

00:26.790 --> 00:30.090
Can you understand this fear, Ouka?

01:03.540 --> 01:06.040
Stop it!

01:15.050 --> 01:16.570
Stop this right now.

01:16.570 --> 01:18.490
If not, I will shoot you!

01:18.840 --> 01:19.870
That's the way.

01:19.870 --> 01:23.030
I'm the Child of Enka who will bring about the end of humankind.

01:23.030 --> 01:24.800
Kill me, Ouka.

01:24.800 --> 01:26.600
That's your mission.

01:46.330 --> 01:51.340
Kyouka. I don't believe that you're actually considering humanity's well-being.

01:52.570 --> 01:56.950
You just want to kill the Child of Enka that follows this family like a spectre.

01:57.250 --> 01:58.590
That's what you actually want, isn't it?

02:00.490 --> 02:02.300
In a way, it's very much like you.

02:11.910 --> 02:16.360
That's how important this family has become to you.

02:16.720 --> 02:17.850
To me, as well.

02:19.610 --> 02:22.050
But this isn't the right way to achieve it.

02:23.550 --> 02:26.790
So I must stop you!

02:26.790 --> 02:31.510
You're the one who said, "What kind of parent points a gun at their child?" to me.

02:31.510 --> 02:34.810
Yet now, you're making me point a gun at you?

02:34.810 --> 02:37.800
You're making me point a gun at my dear wife?

02:53.940 --> 02:55.150
Wait, Dad!

02:55.150 --> 02:56.010
Yuuka!

02:56.690 --> 03:00.560
I kept it a secret, but I'm the Child of Enka.

03:09.910 --> 03:12.690
See? All the monkeys are listening to me.

03:14.650 --> 03:19.380
Plus, I once did a horrible thing to Oasis-san under the influence of Water!

03:19.900 --> 03:23.920
I thought that I might have been dreaming, but I wasn't.

03:27.890 --> 03:32.560
Just like that, I get manipulated by something else and lose myself!

03:33.400 --> 03:36.820
So I am the Child of Enka who puts this family in danger!

03:36.820 --> 03:39.690
I am simply the enemy of this family!

03:39.690 --> 03:41.360
Obey me, monkeys!

03:41.880 --> 03:42.740
Teika-kun?

03:44.780 --> 03:45.570
Teika?

03:46.550 --> 03:50.730
I can control any animal on Earth with one howl.

03:50.730 --> 03:53.420
This is evidence of me being the dreadful Child of Enka!

03:53.420 --> 03:56.810
You might have the power, but you have a kind heart.

03:57.240 --> 04:00.800
I always carry a temper in me.

04:00.800 --> 04:03.720
It goes out of control at times,
and there is a possibility of me not being me.

04:04.220 --> 04:06.880
If that's true, then I am the Child of Enka!

04:06.880 --> 04:11.350
Since I am both male and female inside my body.

04:11.350 --> 04:13.290
No, I think you're stretching this one...

04:13.290 --> 04:14.940
Swaying one way...

04:14.940 --> 04:16.170
Swaying the other way...

04:16.170 --> 04:17.920
I'm so unstable.

04:17.920 --> 04:20.190
Who knows when I'll turn around and harm humans.

04:20.190 --> 04:22.910
If you say that, then I'm the daughter of the Himemiya, the family of Oni.

04:22.910 --> 04:25.700
Inside of me lives a scary Oni...

04:25.700 --> 04:28.580
You don't have the gene to be the Child of Enka, do you?

04:28.580 --> 04:29.660
The most dangerous one would be...

04:31.340 --> 04:33.040
Me.

04:33.080 --> 04:34.200
I'm the one!

04:34.200 --> 04:35.140
No, it's me!

04:35.140 --> 04:36.080
I said me!

04:37.460 --> 04:39.090
Just agree with me!

04:40.340 --> 04:41.340
It's me.

04:44.430 --> 04:45.970
All of you, stop fighting!

04:50.430 --> 04:53.000
Ouka. Laugh at me.

04:53.850 --> 04:57.690
Who would have thought this Kyouka-sama would choose to die for someone else...

04:57.690 --> 05:02.660
But Ouka... I'm still happy to go.

05:03.440 --> 05:05.200
You may be satisfied with that.

05:05.200 --> 05:07.200
But what about everyone else?!

05:07.200 --> 05:08.770
You're cheating, Mom!

05:08.770 --> 05:10.560
You always take the best parts!

05:10.560 --> 05:12.290
Are we powerless?!

05:12.290 --> 05:13.430
Mother!

05:13.430 --> 05:14.210
Mother!

05:16.310 --> 05:19.630
Mother. Do you hear everyone's voice?

05:19.630 --> 05:22.440
A family is no longer a family if even one goes missing.

05:22.950 --> 05:25.420
Everyone needs you.

05:26.930 --> 05:28.050
Ouka!

05:28.050 --> 05:29.360
Stop it everyone!

05:32.350 --> 05:33.890
Mom?

05:39.560 --> 05:40.520
Kyouka?

05:40.520 --> 05:41.770
Mom!

05:58.290 --> 05:59.290
Kyouka!

06:13.810 --> 06:16.110
Guys! Where are you looking?!

06:16.110 --> 06:17.660
Your Kyouka-sama is over here!

06:18.040 --> 06:18.940
Kyouka?

06:18.940 --> 06:20.100
Who is...

06:21.810 --> 06:22.940
...who?

06:24.600 --> 06:28.070
You're my children, and you can't tell who your mother is?

06:28.700 --> 06:31.570
She's right! This Kitty has the ears.

06:31.570 --> 06:33.400
Eye for an eye. Tooth for a tooth.

06:33.400 --> 06:35.580
When you get hijacked, hijack back!

06:35.580 --> 06:40.500
Unfortunately, no one's better than Kyouka-sama when it comes to taking over another's body.

06:40.500 --> 06:42.000
Mom!

06:43.520 --> 06:44.750
You're so soft!

06:44.750 --> 06:46.180
It's really our Mother!

06:46.180 --> 06:47.100
Kitty!

06:47.100 --> 06:48.130
Mother!

06:48.130 --> 06:48.800
Mother!

06:48.800 --> 06:51.800
Stop it, guys. You'll squash me.

06:52.660 --> 06:53.760
Kyouka.

06:53.760 --> 06:55.000
O-Ouka.

06:56.240 --> 06:58.430
Isn't there something you should say?

06:58.790 --> 07:00.300
He's right, Mother.

07:02.600 --> 07:04.660
Sorry I made you worry...

07:05.820 --> 07:07.290
I can't hear you well.

07:07.940 --> 07:09.950
Sorry I made you worry!

07:14.650 --> 07:17.290
Thank you for coming back to us.

07:24.730 --> 07:27.630
I'll absorb them so they can never do any more harm.

07:29.550 --> 07:32.790
Well, the water's danger is out of the way, so let's go home.

07:32.790 --> 07:35.170
We still have Gekka's marriage to figure out.

07:35.170 --> 07:36.540
Marriage?!

07:36.540 --> 07:37.430
What is that?!

07:40.720 --> 07:43.980
I feel like I've seen this before.

07:53.940 --> 07:55.030
So he's...

07:55.030 --> 07:56.820
Gekka's groom?

07:57.680 --> 08:00.160
Nice to meet you. This is my card.

08:00.160 --> 08:02.080
Gouyokuou?

08:02.080 --> 08:03.980
Gouyokuou?

08:02.080 --> 08:03.980
Here. Hello. Nice to meet you.

08:03.980 --> 08:08.160
Gouyokuou as in the alien who will destroy Earth based on Enka's last words?

08:08.160 --> 08:12.110
No. I have no intention of destroying the Earth.

08:12.110 --> 08:16.260
He is the very person that brought those stinky slimy eggs.

08:16.260 --> 08:17.990
That's dangerous. Can I kill him?

08:26.000 --> 08:26.770
I'm sorry!

08:26.770 --> 08:29.100
Little- or would you be my big brother?

08:29.100 --> 08:33.410
All I want is approval to be married to Gekka, and instead I've hurt the family!

08:33.410 --> 08:34.530
Stupid, stupid, stupid me!

08:37.030 --> 08:41.190
The biggest problem is anything he wishes for comes true.

08:41.190 --> 08:45.790
That's why he willingly wears those restraining rods.

08:45.790 --> 08:52.590
But while I was waiting for Gekka, lots of them came off in order to protect myself from the Earthlings' attacks.

08:52.590 --> 08:54.650
I only have one left!

08:54.650 --> 08:58.360
If this one comes off, this planet will explode!

08:58.360 --> 09:00.430
Being too strong is a problem, eh?

09:00.430 --> 09:02.980
So Gekka, grant my wish!

09:02.980 --> 09:05.110
Please marry me!

09:08.610 --> 09:09.110
Gekka!

09:09.740 --> 09:12.570
You can't accept a threat-like proposal like that!

09:12.570 --> 09:13.780
No, Father-

09:13.780 --> 09:16.110
You have no right to call me "Father"!

09:16.110 --> 09:17.680
I'm not threatening her.

09:17.680 --> 09:19.690
I really love Gekka.

09:19.690 --> 09:21.060
Gouyokuou...

09:21.060 --> 09:27.000
Gekka. It's outrageous of you to marry Gouyokuou out of self-sacrifice to save the Earth.

09:27.000 --> 09:28.000
Father...

09:28.000 --> 09:29.500
Hold it right there!

09:29.500 --> 09:33.060
Ouka! You shouldn't speak the God's heart for her!

09:33.060 --> 09:34.090
Oasis-san?

09:36.400 --> 09:41.970
God. Are you thinking of reluctantly marrying Gouyokuou for the sake of the Earth?

09:41.970 --> 09:45.180
Or is it that you actually love Gouyokuou?

09:45.180 --> 09:48.850
Or do you not care about him at all?

09:50.730 --> 09:52.930
Make it clear!

09:52.930 --> 09:54.960
Say it out loud in front of everyone!

09:54.960 --> 09:58.110
You're not part of the family!
Why are you taking part in this?!

09:58.110 --> 10:00.410
You've all forgotten the most important thing.

10:00.410 --> 10:02.630
It doesn't matter who thinks what.

10:02.950 --> 10:05.870
If Gouyokuou doesn't like the idea, then it doesn't pass.

10:05.870 --> 10:08.540
After all, no one can beat him.

10:08.540 --> 10:09.680
Mother?

10:10.080 --> 10:13.180
In other words, make Gouyokuou side with you, and you win.

10:13.180 --> 10:14.840
This isn't a matter of win or lose.

10:15.090 --> 10:18.120
I call this, "Let's all play the Greed game!"

10:18.580 --> 10:19.980
Game?!

10:28.350 --> 10:30.230
The rules are simple!

10:30.230 --> 10:34.610
The one who presents a future that Gouyokuou likes most wins.

10:34.610 --> 10:36.800
The future will become exactly like that.

10:39.610 --> 10:44.120
I thought she'd become saner after strengthening her bond with the family, but...

10:44.120 --> 10:46.840
To settle one's daughter's marriage through a game?

10:46.840 --> 10:49.330
That's the Kitty we're used to seeing.

10:49.330 --> 10:53.540
Amazing. If we can settle this peacefully, then I would love to.

10:53.540 --> 10:56.380
Please come up with a future where everyone's happy!

10:56.380 --> 11:02.890
Do you hear that?! If you want to win, then come up with a plan for the future that he would like the most!

11:02.890 --> 11:04.390
Team A!

11:04.390 --> 11:06.540
Kyouka-sama and the Midarezaki family!

11:07.610 --> 11:11.240
The future we present is, we'll allow the marriage between Gekka and Gouyokuou.

11:11.240 --> 11:14.570
However when they do get married, we'll have them live on Earth.

11:15.610 --> 11:17.490
But Gekka never said she'd marry!

11:17.490 --> 11:18.280
Shut up!

11:20.040 --> 11:23.430
What makes you think a parent can butt into their child's love affair?!

11:23.430 --> 11:25.280
This goes for Hyouka and the Pachinko girl, too!

11:25.280 --> 11:26.200
We're not in a relation-

11:27.300 --> 11:28.660
This goes for Teika and Madara, too!

11:28.660 --> 11:30.430
Madara and I are not in that kind of relation-

11:32.180 --> 11:33.260
Why?!

11:34.040 --> 11:37.840
If Gekka likes the idea,
then there is no reason for her not to marry.

11:37.840 --> 11:42.460
But it looks like Gekka isn't too sure yet,
so let's start from square one of the relationship.

11:42.460 --> 11:43.780
Mother...

11:44.600 --> 11:47.030
So we get to stay with Gekka?!

11:47.030 --> 11:51.260
If so, the Water wouldn't have a problem, so it might be a very peaceful resolution.

11:51.260 --> 11:53.440
If you would support this future,

11:53.440 --> 11:57.230
Gekka said she'd do any one thing you ask her to.

11:59.370 --> 12:00.630
Hey, Mother!

12:00.630 --> 12:01.390
I never-

12:02.610 --> 12:04.590
No way! That Gekka would?!

12:04.590 --> 12:07.540
The Gekka who's made of pride would do anything I ask?!

12:07.540 --> 12:10.160
If you say, "I was joking" later,

12:10.160 --> 12:12.790
even I would get mad!

12:11.660 --> 12:12.790
I'm not joking.

12:12.790 --> 12:16.570
From a lovey-dovey date with holding hands to...

12:15.500 --> 12:16.960
You're under arrest!

12:17.390 --> 12:19.780
...a kiss on the cheek.

12:20.510 --> 12:27.330
Since there are kids here, I can't say it explicitly, but all this and that are welcome, too!

12:28.990 --> 12:32.910
You guys! I'm absolutely touched by the future you came up with!

12:32.910 --> 12:36.270
If it's an amazing future like this,
then there's no way I wouldn't support it!

12:36.270 --> 12:38.680
So how many point does the Team A get?

12:39.820 --> 12:43.150
One hundred ninety-five million
eight thousand five hundred points!

12:43.710 --> 12:46.550
It's an astronomical number right off the bat!

12:46.550 --> 12:48.910
I guess Gouyokuou is a man after all.

12:48.910 --> 12:50.910
He's just a simple-minded idiot.

12:55.010 --> 12:57.680
Team B. Oasis!

12:58.200 --> 13:00.840
We'll listen to the future you think of, too.

13:00.840 --> 13:02.170
Though I think it's meaningless.

13:02.790 --> 13:05.320
The Team B's... What I wish for is...

13:05.320 --> 13:08.300
Rather, the future I imagine is...

13:08.300 --> 13:09.680
I allow the marriage.

13:10.910 --> 13:15.850
But, I won't allow them to be on Earth.

13:16.650 --> 13:21.610
It should be evident from these events that Gouyokuou is a source of disaster.

13:21.610 --> 13:28.410
How many people lost their houses to fire, how many cities were razed, and how much chaos came about because of you?

13:30.080 --> 13:32.760
If you want to marry her, go ahead.

13:32.760 --> 13:37.580
But this planet is too fragile for you to live on.

13:37.580 --> 13:42.150
Too weak and fragile.
Anyone can come up with that answer.

13:43.300 --> 13:45.080
It's no time for you to be depressed!

13:45.080 --> 13:46.920
She just denied your existence!

13:46.920 --> 13:47.890
Why don't you say something?!

13:51.200 --> 13:54.900
But getting married and going to space with them is a little...

13:54.900 --> 13:56.870
I'm not sure if Gekka would agree.

13:56.870 --> 13:59.860
She's part of Operation Something or Another right now.

13:59.860 --> 14:03.690
I'd feel guilty taking her in the middle of that
and whisking her off into space.

14:03.690 --> 14:05.730
It can be taken care of!

14:06.400 --> 14:10.320
We, Aquatician, were part of the God's body originally.

14:10.320 --> 14:11.610
In other words, we're her double.

14:11.610 --> 14:17.370
So one of us can stay behind and take her spot in the Operation Cozy Family.

14:17.370 --> 14:18.540
Replace Gekka?

14:18.540 --> 14:19.670
Me.

14:19.670 --> 14:23.630
I can take part in Operation Cozy Family.

14:23.630 --> 14:24.830
Oasis...

14:25.230 --> 14:26.630
You...

14:27.070 --> 14:29.050
I love Ouka.

14:30.270 --> 14:32.710
I want to stay with Ouka.

14:33.130 --> 14:35.290
I noticed after Gouyokuou told me...

14:35.800 --> 14:37.680
...that this emotion is love.

14:38.560 --> 14:41.000
But love is difficult.

14:41.350 --> 14:43.780
Just being close to him is lonely.

14:44.280 --> 14:47.600
I wish that Ouka would look at me, too.

14:48.690 --> 14:51.130
The plan isn't going the way I thought...

14:51.130 --> 14:51.970
I'm sorry!

14:52.580 --> 14:55.370
I cannot answer to your feelings.

14:55.370 --> 14:57.580
Who would turn one down so easily?

14:57.580 --> 15:01.080
I have a beloved wife and a family I want to protect.

15:03.710 --> 15:04.590
So...

15:05.190 --> 15:06.210
I'm sorry!

15:08.370 --> 15:11.740
Gouyokuou... What you think no longer holds any meaning!

15:11.740 --> 15:13.410
I win this game!

15:13.830 --> 15:15.600
Oasis-san, what are you saying?

15:15.600 --> 15:18.210
You have a debt to repay!

15:19.550 --> 15:21.150
Oh yeah, I do!

15:21.450 --> 15:23.650
You helped me.

15:24.450 --> 15:28.920
I asked her to lend the Water's strength to save this city.

15:28.920 --> 15:32.030
So that rain happened thanks to Gouyokuou-san?

15:36.110 --> 15:38.490
I must repay the debt.

15:38.490 --> 15:40.010
I must return the favor.

15:47.420 --> 15:48.340
Watch out!

15:57.750 --> 15:58.560
Gekka!

15:59.930 --> 16:02.030
Sorry for the trouble.

16:04.760 --> 16:05.820
Gekka!

16:17.770 --> 16:22.490
Gouyokuou. You're not actually under Oasis' influence, are you?

16:24.270 --> 16:25.570
I know you well.

16:25.570 --> 16:30.090
You're loyal, fair, and diligent to the point of being a fool.

16:30.090 --> 16:34.400
Why does it hurt to just say what you think?

16:34.400 --> 16:38.100
This world won't change through love.

16:38.100 --> 16:45.570
The words you managed to say do not even have the power of a ripple in space.

16:45.900 --> 16:47.760
And that's probably why it's frustrating.

16:48.260 --> 16:54.560
Yet, Oasis. You didn't run away. You faced the issue head on.

16:56.290 --> 16:58.000
I'm the weak one.

16:58.360 --> 17:00.670
Although Mother knew it all along.

17:01.420 --> 17:11.980
Through the Greed Game, she gave me a push on my back, since I don't know how to rely on or trust others fully.

17:12.510 --> 17:14.560
She's always been like that.

17:16.010 --> 17:17.480
Say, Gouyokuou.

17:17.930 --> 17:19.250
What is it, Gekka?

17:19.250 --> 17:25.750
The fact that you came to my planet that's like a drop of water in this universe...

17:25.750 --> 17:27.340
That fact that I was able to see you...

17:27.340 --> 17:29.150
I was really happy.

17:30.450 --> 17:35.120
Back then, it was my first time meeting someone that was not me, so I ran away in fear.

17:35.120 --> 17:39.100
I only said I'd give an answer
one thousand years later to get away.

17:40.160 --> 17:43.750
But you kept your promise.

17:43.750 --> 17:44.970
You're a fine man.

17:44.970 --> 17:47.170
You're too good for me.

17:48.670 --> 17:50.720
I love you.

17:52.580 --> 17:53.670
Gekka...

17:54.520 --> 17:57.590
Thank you. It's so great to hear that word.

17:58.790 --> 18:04.230
But to think it over, I was just a bother.

18:04.230 --> 18:07.640
I've caused so much trouble to the Earthlings.

18:08.480 --> 18:12.000
I don't want to cause any more trouble for them.

18:12.310 --> 18:15.570
If I stay here, I might destroy it by accident.

18:16.770 --> 18:20.200
But you can't leave this place yet, right?

18:20.200 --> 18:21.560
Gouyokuou...

18:22.080 --> 18:24.440
It's fine. I'm used to waiting.

18:24.840 --> 18:28.580
So could you send me far away with your teleportation?

18:32.820 --> 18:36.990
I'll remember how this hand feels and travel through space.

18:37.500 --> 18:39.980
Slowly, taking thousands of years.

18:40.430 --> 18:42.930
Then, I promise to come see you again.

18:44.240 --> 18:47.400
When I do, will you marry me then?

18:48.960 --> 18:49.560
Yes.

18:58.070 --> 19:02.870
My beloved who found me in this vast universe.

19:02.870 --> 19:04.910
I won't have you wait alone.

19:07.120 --> 19:09.540
I will also wait for that moment.

19:09.540 --> 19:10.380
On this planet.

19:11.380 --> 19:12.290
Gouyokuou.

19:13.380 --> 19:16.510
I'll look forward to meeting you again.

19:18.510 --> 19:21.660
I've done a horrible thing to you.

19:22.170 --> 19:25.190
I can't stop your tears.

19:26.000 --> 19:27.930
But I can be your partner to talk with.

19:28.520 --> 19:29.890
Little at a time is fine.

19:29.890 --> 19:31.250
Say what you feel.

19:31.770 --> 19:35.280
Once you get over it, I'm sure you'll be able to find another wonderful love.

19:37.280 --> 19:40.030
But... Right now, let me cry.

19:44.220 --> 19:49.770
Gouyokuou leaves the Earth, and the expected doom ends with the Midarezaki family's great work.

20:00.050 --> 20:11.000
The mystery of the Child of Enka still remains, but the Midarezaki have repelled the Water and have proven their strong family bond.

20:00.050 --> 20:03.070
Keep your hands moving!

20:03.600 --> 20:04.550
Mujyakey-sama!

20:08.110 --> 20:09.560
It's ready.

20:11.990 --> 20:15.940
This shall support the resumption of Operation Cozy Family.

20:15.940 --> 20:18.440
"This shall support the resumption of..."

20:19.520 --> 20:24.530
Wait. Could Million-sama have expected all of this from the beginning and have given them those trials?

20:29.040 --> 20:30.770
Raichou-chan.

20:30.770 --> 20:32.270
Show that one to me again.

20:32.700 --> 20:33.880
I'll draw it.

20:37.300 --> 20:39.830
It can't be! Not from that stupid Million!

20:39.830 --> 20:41.460
I will get her back one day!

20:41.460 --> 20:43.430
Maybe I'll draw eyes on her eyelids while she's asleep.

20:43.430 --> 20:44.270
That's not enough!

20:44.270 --> 20:47.060
I'll humiliate you more than you've humiliated me!

20:44.270 --> 20:47.060
Million-sama has come to totally love the stomach face.

20:51.770 --> 20:54.440
I wonder what Oasis-san is doing now.

20:54.440 --> 20:55.520
Are you worried about her?

20:55.520 --> 20:58.640
I think I understand Oasis-san's feeling.

20:58.640 --> 21:02.280
Everyone's lonely and wishes to be wanted by someone.

21:02.280 --> 21:04.740
But that's not limited to love.

21:04.740 --> 21:06.490
It applies to family, too.

21:06.490 --> 21:08.990
But we're not lonely anymore.

21:08.990 --> 21:12.370
Since we have a family that seeks one another.

21:13.730 --> 21:15.360
Hey, where's Kyouka?

21:17.900 --> 21:18.830
Kyouka!

21:18.830 --> 21:20.400
Damn, he found me.

21:20.400 --> 21:21.920
Where are you going?

21:22.470 --> 21:24.840
To go take care of something I left.

21:24.840 --> 21:27.480
I thought I'd go and take care of it.

21:28.390 --> 21:30.970
Are you going to the underground empire?

21:30.970 --> 21:32.000
Mom?

21:32.000 --> 21:36.170
Look. This is why I tried to sneak out. It's all your fault.

21:36.170 --> 21:39.770
When I see tears and get begged at time like this, my determination wavers.

21:39.770 --> 21:41.070
We won't stop you.

21:41.070 --> 21:43.140
What? So you don't mind me gone?

21:43.140 --> 21:45.570
More like, you don't need me around?

21:45.570 --> 21:49.940
Don't you want to stay with me or cuddle with me all the time?

21:49.940 --> 21:51.230
Are those serious questions?

21:51.230 --> 21:53.330
No, I just wanted to say 'em.

21:53.330 --> 21:56.730
Even if we're apart, no matter what happens, Kyouka...

21:56.730 --> 21:59.340
Your home is here, right?

22:00.840 --> 22:01.930
Yeah...

22:02.240 --> 22:03.440
You're right!

22:04.260 --> 22:06.270
Have a safe trip, Mom!

22:07.010 --> 22:08.180
I'm off!

23:24.410 --> 23:26.170
Don't think this is the end!

23:26.170 --> 23:27.750
This frenzy party will last forever!

23:27.750 --> 23:28.900
I just decided that it will!

23:28.900 --> 23:30.420
"Will that be all right?" you ask?

23:30.420 --> 23:33.340
Rest assured! As a most wonderful fact, I, Kyouka-sama, am omniscient and omnipotent!

23:38.840 --> 23:41.100
I thought you'd left.

23:42.610 --> 23:44.110
They're so annoying.

23:44.110 --> 23:48.610
You think this Kyouka-sama would make you guys experience a lonely time?

23:48.860 --> 23:52.900
Rest assured. As a most wonderful fact, I, Kyouka-sama, am omniscient and omnipotent!
